{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups","id":1203915,"title":"What are your Outcaste groups?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-06T11:39:26-07:00","id":1203915,"title":"What are your Outcaste groups?","content":"So, the current preview introduced a bunch of cool Outcaste groups. What new groups have they inspired in you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T20:39:06-07:00","id":1204088,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking about a couple of cultures of DB Beastmen descended from loyalists who kept serving the Lunars. They\u2019re rare, but I think logically would exist. I\u2019m think bat-people in the southeastern jungle, and Komodo Dragon Blooded (... get it?) in the Caul.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t know were yet, but i\u2019m imaginging a remote kingdom where tribal entity is tied to Aspect. When a Dragon-Blooded Exalts they are always married into their Aspect Tribe, regardless of their ancestry. And the five tribes control territories appropriate to their respective elements, and engage in contests of ritual combat for dominance every few years.<br /> <br /> A culture of pelagrathropes and dolphin-people with Dragon-Blooded in their Bloodlines, charged as ancient hunters and guardians of the deeps to patrol against the returns of the Spoken - though that original duty has faded into distant myth as they cling to their identity as sacred hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:22:57-07:00","id":1204097,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I had thoughts on the decendants of Loyalists too. I wonder how many people here have variations on that theme","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T22:18:22-07:00","id":1204107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204097#post1204097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I had thoughts on the decendants of Loyalists too. I wonder how many people here have variations on that theme</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had a cult dedicated to a Prescence Supernal Solar's sacred texts in the South East, currently operating as a secret society to overthrowParsad and restore their Solar order (Said Solar in life was an autocratic fascist, so...these were a villian group). Primarily Fire and Earth aspect, thematics of animal-armors. They cultivated mortal warriors in their mountain regions and followed a patrilineage, resulting in their cult spreading strangely across families in Parsaad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T08:11:49-07:00","id":1204186,"title":"","content":"So, the game I ran until recently (and now my friend's running) has two main Outcaste groups.<br /> <br /> One is a country called Varamaya, where humans are split into 5 social castes, one for each aspect, led by a small number of DBs of that aspect.<br /> So the Tree Caste are vegetarian, pacifist polyamorous farmers;<br /> The Flame Caste are ecstatic warrior-berzerkers and butchers;<br /> The Wind Caste are artisans;<br /> The River Caste are river traders (the country is surrounded by many rivers and lakes);<br /> The Stone Caste are labourers and miners.<br /> There are about 10 DBs altogether; not a big number, but over hundreds of years these families have moulded the entire society in their image. It's believed that following the way of one caste helps you exalt as a particular aspect. The DBs only reproduce within their own Caste, meaning that, a majority of the time, exalts of a particular Aspect are from their own caste, though not always. As the blood has weakened, it is has become more awkward for the DBs to keep their blood potency amongst their own Aspect, leading to a number of theological arguments.<br /> <br /> In the end, this culture ended up allying with the Realm (they were anti-Realm and allied with Harborhead, but the PCs topped Harborhead's government, and Varayama discovered that the anti-Realm operations against them were actually the PCs in disguise, so they switched to the Realm).<br /> <br /> <br /> The Four Kingdoms were once ruled by an inter-married set of DB families. Inheritance is matrilineal, and the Queens fulfill important religious and cultural duties, while their husbands lead the country in war and diplomacy. They rule a variety of ethnic clans, bound to the Queens by oaths. The Queens themselves follow a form of Dragon-Worship, as do some of the clans, but others worship local Gods and consider the Queens the Gods' representatives (ensured by the Queens with sacrifices to the local Gods).<br /> <br /> But the weakening of the families' blood has caused the system to break down. Many of the Queens are only &quot;Dragonblooded&quot; as a legal fiction. They attempt to marry foreign Outcaste men (with the promise of getting to be a King) to infuse the families with DB blood again, but there aren't enough available.<br /> At the beginning of the game:<br /> One kingdom was ruled by a mortal and her Cloud Person-Blood husband, who pretended to be an Air Aspect;<br /> One kingdom was ruled by a mortal and her mutant sea-person husband, who named himself Aquos Daanadsson, and claimed to be a Water Aspect;<br /> One kingdom was ruled by a Fire Aspect called Ashen Witch and her toyboy puppet husband;<br /> The last kingdom was in theory ruled by two mortals pretending to be DBs, but the real power was the Queen's father and ex-King (who was no longer King because his wife had died), an Earth Aspect.<br /> <br /> But after the PCs went through, the Cloud Person-Blooded king was divorced by his wife, Aquos's wife was killed by PCs who made Aquos their puppet, but then Ashen Witch divorced her husband, married Aquos, and took his kingdom (which she inherited as the old Queen was her second cousin), making him her puppet, and leaving her old kingdom to her daughter, who she managed to marry to a Wood Aspect adventurer. The other kingdoms rulers were all killed (either by PCs or the Realm) and one of the PCs (whose married to Ashen Witch's other daughter) has seized control of it.<br /> So, basically one particular Fire-Aspected Queen managed to rise to pre-eminence, but she's still at the mercy of the PCs, and she's still ruling with a fake-DB husband, as having more &quot;DBs&quot; gives greater cultural control.<br /> <br /> You can see the key theme of both of these sets of Outcastes was the thinning of the blood, and how Dragonblood families whose right to rule depends on their Exalted blood would try and cope with this, from a societal and legal perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-07-2018, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:09:51-07:00","id":1204197,"title":"","content":"I'm still toying with an idea of a 'bandit clan' of Outcastes who get up to various shady dealings throughout the Hundred Kingdoms. I keep not being sure on how legitimate to make them though. Are they purely bandits, thieves and criminals, are they more mercenaries and heroes for hire, do they straddle the line? Oddly, trying to work out what they do has been my biggest stumbling block in developing the group further","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T10:58:46-07:00","id":1204224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204197#post1204197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still toying with an idea of a 'bandit clan' of Outcastes who get up to various shady dealings throughout the Hundred Kingdoms. I keep not being sure on how legitimate to make them though. Are they purely bandits, thieves and criminals, are they more mercenaries and heroes for hire, do they straddle the line? Oddly, trying to work out what they do has been my biggest stumbling block in developing the group further</div> </div> </div> </div>That kinda sounds like the Grass Spiders already!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T12:38:12-07:00","id":1204258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204224#post1204224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kinda sounds like the Grass Spiders already!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They're a good starting point. I'm looking to take a bit of a family vibe to them. They've been legendary bandits and raiders for generations, they strike deals with greedy rulers, and face overwhelming odds with smiles and laughter. I also am considering a tradition where the young members come of age by venturing out into the world, and their name is the first thing people call them. Like, Lightning Blade, Holy Tornado, Great Mountain....<br /> <br /> And of course, one guy made kinda a fool of himself attacking a Lookshyan camp, so his name is Baka. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:41:21-07:00","id":1204296,"title":"","content":"Anyone imagine a group of Loyalists who control territory? Or is it all secret societies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:54:18-07:00","id":1204306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204296#post1204296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone imagine a group of Loyalists who control territory? Or is it all secret societies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would have had to have survived not just the the last 8 centuries, but the entirety of the Shogunate, so I think it's limited to deep Threshold &quot;barbarian&quot; kingdoms under the patronage of the Silver Pact - hence my image of it being Beastmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T15:16:06-07:00","id":1204313,"title":"","content":"*hums* Something in the Underworld, perhaps? Or remote North. The Isolated Mountain Community is a bit of a classic, if you're going with something that survived. Or perhaps a group founded and trained by the Cult of the Illuminated, to give their lives for their sparkly overlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:11:49-07:00","id":1204328,"title":"","content":"A family of Water DBs in the west, acting as privateers and pirates for hire for any faction that can pay. The secret is that they are actually a group of Peleps plants, who are there to infiltrate and untangle the web of alliances between western powers, to prepare the way for Peleps to move out to the west to escape the civil war.<br /> <br /> I'm planning to run a chronicle for my wife once the book is ready, where she is a DB pirate out west, and have her uncover evidence of Peleps preparing for their exodus, and see what she does with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","name":"Spacepup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:41:33-07:00","id":1204336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacepup</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204328#post1204328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A family of Water DBs in the west, acting as privateers and pirates for hire for any faction that can pay. The secret is that they are actually a group of Peleps plants, who are there to infiltrate and untangle the web of alliances between western powers, to prepare the way for Peleps to move out to the west to escape the civil war.<br /> <br /> I'm planning to run a chronicle for my wife once the book is ready, where she is a DB pirate out west, and have her uncover evidence of Peleps preparing for their exodus, and see what she does with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! V\u2019Neef could make an interesting ally there. That sounds like a fun chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:13:20-07:00","id":1204364,"title":"","content":"How about ynderground in an abandoned mountain folk cavern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T19:49:19-07:00","id":1204395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204364#post1204364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about ynderground in an abandoned mountain folk cavern?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've thought about a group of Dragon-Blooded Underfolk.... but part of me wants to wait till we see what the Mountain Folk are like and up to in 3E before exploring the topic at all, since I have no idea if the Nameless War is still even a thing, so the context they'd be living in is pretty much a complete mystery at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T20:07:23-07:00","id":1204397,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...<br /> <br /> \u200bHow about a.. travelling theatrical troupe... dedicated to preservation and dissemination of ancient and historical lore... with a sideline in consultancy, troubleshooting and human computational services?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T21:13:43-07:00","id":1204414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204395#post1204395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've thought about a group of Dragon-Blooded Underfolk.... but part of me wants to wait till we see what the Mountain Folk are like and up to in 3E before exploring the topic at all, since I have no idea if the Nameless War is still even a thing, so the context they'd be living in is pretty much a complete mystery at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably a good idea<br /> <br /> Still, I think a bloodline out somewhere that has built a small kingdom waiting for their former Solar patron to return wouuld be fun. Esp when said Solar reincarnates as nothing like they were expecting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T21:53:27-07:00","id":1204429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204364#post1204364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about ynderground in an abandoned mountain folk cavern?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204395#post1204395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've thought about a group of Dragon-Blooded Underfolk.... but part of me wants to wait till we see what the Mountain Folk are like and up to in 3E before exploring the topic at all, since I have no idea if the Nameless War is still even a thing, so the context they'd be living in is pretty much a complete mystery at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are underground regions that may have little to do with the Mountain Folk, such as the caverns of Jau Dei (a Ragara garisonned satrapy). Or is this idea specifically about a (literally) underground outcaste group in the Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:19:22-07:00","id":1204486,"title":"","content":"You know, if there's one thing that I think the book emphasized about outcastes, it would be their agency and dignity as members of the dominant Exalted of the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo it feels kind of odd that for many people, their first response when it comes to devising groups of their own is &quot;serve the Lunar Exalted&quot;. Like, not even a particular kind of thing that they might do for them, that emphasizes unique skills, just serve a Celestial Exalt, and maybe be beastfolk.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be one thing if it was a group that were a Lunar's actual children, maybe from a backstory of that Lunar also being somebody with the Dragon's blood (possibly even a former member of the Scarlet Dynasty) who paired up with another outcaste, but no, they're &quot;loyalists&quot;, soooo I take it that they're supposed to have been under a Lunar since the Usurpation?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do they get out of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-08-2018, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:36:18-07:00","id":1204489,"title":"","content":"which is why mine are not subject to any Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T06:00:39-07:00","id":1204519,"title":"","content":"I think them being devoted to a Solar still fulfils Isator's point. And I kind of thought the same as Isator reading this thread (my own Outcaste groups were anti-Solar).<br /> <br /> Not that I want to tell people &quot;Bad-wrong-fun.&quot; If you want to have an Outcaste group devoted to an ancient religion of shiny god-kings you can. I'd personally be tempted to do something with it whereby 1500 years of religious drift and evolution has caused them to have a very, very weird view of what a Solar is.<br /> <br /> I might do that in a Realm game.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't for a Solar game though. Bit too easy. That's why all my Outcaste groups have been a bit anti-Solar, so that they're a challenge for PCs to overcome... but not as much as the Realm, so they can still try diplomacy, rather than just violence.<br /> <br /> (They mostly just intimidated people in the end, and killed those who were mostly overtly against them, but I guess that's a bit more interesting than just fighting the Wyld Hunt yet again.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T06:20:00-07:00","id":1204524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204519#post1204519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think them being devoted to a Solar still fulfils Isator's point. And I kind of thought the same as Isator reading this thread (my own Outcaste groups were anti-Solar).<br /> <br /> Not that I want to tell people &amp;quot;Bad-wrong-fun.&amp;quot; If you want to have an Outcaste group devoted to an ancient religion of shiny god-kings you can. I'd personally be tempted to do something with it whereby 1500 years of religious drift and evolution has caused them to have a very, very weird view of what a Solar is.<br /> <br /> I might do that in a Realm game.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't for a Solar game though. Bit too easy. That's why all my Outcaste groups have been a bit anti-Solar, so that they're a challenge for PCs to overcome... but not as much as the Realm, so they can still try diplomacy, rather than just violence.<br /> <br /> (They mostly just intimidated people in the end, and killed those who were mostly overtly against them, but I guess that's a bit more interesting than just fighting the Wyld Hunt yet again.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My own cult probably didn\u2019t recognize solars as solars and were there as \u201callies\u201d who wanted the Player that unwittingly had their founders exaltation to follow out doctrine he likely would find horrific. I think it creates immediate tension with the realm and other dragonblooded while giving a way for players to find unexpected allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T06:38:02-07:00","id":1204527,"title":"","content":"I actually liked your one, Epee, if I was reading it right as being based on a devotional tradition focused on somebody who happened to be a (presumably long dead) Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T07:38:24-07:00","id":1204541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204486#post1204486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, if there's one thing that I think the book emphasized about outcastes, it would be their agency and dignity as members of the dominant Exalted of the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo it feels kind of odd that for many people, their first response when it comes to devising groups of their own is &quot;serve the Lunar Exalted&quot;. Like, not even a particular kind of thing that they might do for them, that emphasizes unique skills, just serve a Celestial Exalt, and maybe be beastfolk.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be one thing if it was a group that were a Lunar's actual children, maybe from a backstory of that Lunar also being somebody with the Dragon's blood (possibly even a former member of the Scarlet Dynasty) who paired up with another outcaste, but no, they're &quot;loyalists&quot;, soooo I take it that they're supposed to have been under a Lunar since the Usurpation?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do they get out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods, it always feels weird when I agree with you on something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sorry, sorry.<br /> <br /> But yeah. Outcaste groups.lineages need to be more than canon fodder or underlings. They should stand on their own. *hums*<br /> <br /> I'm kinda interested in Outcaste Martial Arts traditions. Terrestrials are the most populous supernatural martial artists, so trying to define some dojos outside the Realm's control seems like an angle. 'City of Martial Artists' sounds gimmicky when you just say that, but so does 'City of Sorcerers'. You can pull it off with some thought IMO *wanders off yonder to ponder*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T07:50:18-07:00","id":1204546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204541#post1204541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gods, it always feels weird when I agree with you on something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do people keep saying this?! Am I so terrible? Am I such a monster that the faintest glimmer of humanity within me is worthy of comment every. Single. Time?<br /> <br /> \u200bBah, to hell with this: I'm going to go off and renew my efforts to seek employment with one of the numerous local companies that does things like make medicine for children with rare diseases.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T07:56:09-07:00","id":1204548,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel any better, I agree with about... 80-90% of the things you say on this forum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-08-2018, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:12:44-07:00","id":1204553,"title":"","content":"It's not about whether or not people agree with me, it's just the message being conveyed when a point of agreement is seen as something worthy of comment upon, and the fact that it's a trend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:23:39-07:00","id":1204558,"title":"","content":"Anyway:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204541#post1204541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda interested in Outcaste Martial Arts traditions. Terrestrials are the most populous supernatural martial artists, so trying to define some dojos outside the Realm's control seems like an angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeees... this is the kind of thing I would have had reservations about in Second Edition, mostly because of the kinds of martial arts that they were generally limited to and because it created such a stark contrast with the many styles that <i>couldn't</i> have such a tradition. Between the fact that the styles that Terrestrials can practice is now basically all of them, and the examples provided by other outcaste groups, it feels like a much stronger idea.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">'City of Martial Artists' sounds gimmicky when you just say that, but so does 'City of Sorcerers'. You can pull it off with some thought IMO *wanders off yonder to ponder*</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHeh, earlier today I was thinking about how some people have been incredulous about Sijan, and comparing that to the real life examples of cities such as Mecca and Vrindavan, as well as a bit to ones that are heavily focused around particular kinds of social industry such as Las Vegas.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yeah, I would say that if a city is the kind where the culture might be expected to place a strong emphasis on martial arts traditions, the municipal government incentivizes or subsidizes them, and they have the added benefit of a couple dozen Exalted spread around a few schools, one could work with the idea that it's a major focus of the city's character and reputation.<br /> <br /> \u200bWould you think of it as something that is pursued for its own sake, as a spiritual endeavour, or is it the kind of thing that might bring in some money? Tournaments that attract people from around the region? Maybe the kind of place where certain belligerent nations send troops intended for a kind of special forces or private guards role to get high-quality training?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:00:20-07:00","id":1204573,"title":"","content":"Something I've kind of observed in my own original setting stuff is a tendency to treat local nobility as almost an extension of the Realm's Patricians, or, better, as what they might be if they didn't have the Dynasty proper looming over them. The wealthy and powerful will likely hoard the blood of the dragons just like more corporeal wealth - I'd be more surprised to <i>not</i> see Outcastes born into royal families.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:32:08-07:00","id":1204587,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the Wanasaan put me in mind of a point about why it might be difficult for many outcaste groups to grow very large; one bad internal dispute (or getting into a nasty fight with an external power), and they'll be driven back to square one.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow I'm suddenly thinking about certain real life religious organisations that have had very strong ideas about growth through adoption or conversion, some to the point where they actually regard procreation as taboo, and I've got the image of a group of outcastes that is very specific about only growing or replacing members through recruiting other outcastes and actually want their bloodlines to end with them, on the logic that sending the Dragon's blood out into the world where it can randomly and unpredictably create Exalted who'll do who knows what with that power is supremely irresponsible. They hold this view even with regards to their own members husbanding their (still possibly poor) progenitive Essence and matching with one another, on a kind of inversion of the logic in the Realm; to them, it's about planning for the event that their hypothetical children <i>won't</i> Exalt, and will carry a strand of the blood into the mortal population.<br /> <br /> I'm seeing something like a cult that kind of splintered away from the Immaculate Order, which looks upon societies like the Realm and even Lookshy favourably because they actually have the resources to sustain large numbers of dedicated Exalted and marshal any outcastes that fall within their spheres, in contrast to the relative disorder of the Threshold and beyond.<br /> <br /> \u200bObviously it's not the kind of thing that could be the central driving conceit of a group of outcastes, and it wouldn't be my first choice for them to be on a kind of crusade against other outcaste societies. Just a detail of their beliefs and practices that would distinguish them from others and has a certain resonance. <br /> <br /> \u200bPerhaps a kind of itinerant group that goes around charitably performing services as needed and as fits the skills of their members, guided by Immaculate ethics (whether it be fighting off Fair Folk or rogue gods, providing medical services or legal advice, performing or helping out towns and villages with some useful construction like a well or a simple defensive wall), with an eye to recruiting any outcastes that they encounter (or at least convincing them of the merits of their position).<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm seeing something like them being founded by a Dynast who, after meeting an outcaste in the Blessed Isle and hearing stories about life in the Threshold, decided to go off adventuring, and after a century or two of that developed a very dim view of what Exalted outside of the Realm were like, returned home to train as an Immaculate monk, and then went back out to perform humble good works and preach his beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:43:01-07:00","id":1204592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204546#post1204546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people keep saying this?! Am I so terrible? Am I such a monster that the faintest glimmer of humanity within me is worthy of comment every. Single. Time?<br /> <br /> \u200bBah, to hell with this: I'm going to go off and renew my efforts to seek employment with one of the numerous local companies that does things like make medicine for children with rare diseases.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204553#post1204553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about whether or not people agree with me, it's just the message being conveyed when a point of agreement is seen as something worthy of comment upon, and the fact that it's a trend.</div> </div> </div> </div>*blinks*<br /> <br /> Erm... wasn't really meaning to imply anything negative. It's just that when I've run into you in the past, it always seemed like it was some debate or another about quality, books or ideas, and we tended to disagree. I always got the impression we liked different things about the setting and had very different tastes (I'm a 2E fan who feels 1E is overly revered, and disliked Glories, Masters of Jade and Shards.) Objectively, there's nothing strange at all about your post and it's not like I viewed it as a change for you. It's just I'm used to running into you on the opposite side of an issue, even where I don't post myself, and wasn't already involved in that bit of the conversation, so chiming in here to echo what you said felt worthy of comment.<br /> <br /> And it's not a bad thing. I guess I'm just used enough to arguing with people on the internet that seeing a sentiment I agree with from someone I'm used to disagreeing with kinda struck me. Sorry if it hit a nerve. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Will get back on topic when I can, busy evening.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:44:46-07:00","id":1204593,"title":"","content":"Never mind all that, tell me more about your idea of a city of martial artists being host to a tradition of Dragon Blooded!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:35:22-07:00","id":1204616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204546#post1204546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do people keep saying this?! Am I so terrible? Am I such a monster that the faintest glimmer of humanity within me is worthy of comment every. Single. Time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, your thing on this forum seems kind of having unusual and novel takes on things that *don't* agree with the average take. Like, more often than, &quot;Yes, I agree with this other poster and the general consensus and it has exactly all the nuances that I believe to exist.&quot; Not like that's a bad thing.<br /> <br /> However, I mean, if that is your thing (the whole originality thing), what % of those takes are gonna be hits for most people reading? Put another way, unless you're the kind of person who spends most of your time agreeing with other people, what are the chances you're the kind of person other people find themselves agreeing with a lot? Maybe think of it as a indirect compliment on your heterodox thinking.<br /> <br /> (If it helps I kind of try to have unusual and novel takes as well, and probably a waaay worse hit rate on here...so... ;-) ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:40:45-07:00","id":1204618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204489#post1204489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which is why mine are not subject to any Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what makes them \u201cloyalists\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:46:12-07:00","id":1204622,"title":"","content":"Eyeyeyey; this isn't about me, it's about the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> \u200bIdea: a group of outcastes based out of the Scavenger Lands who, recognising the value of their services to the Guild and the frequency with which lone Exalted get hired by them, intend to function as a kind of union to give them collective bargaining power with the Guild (at least insofar as they have contacts with the Dirctorate, and what are sure to be some of the more prominent factors and Guild councils), establishing standards by which they're treated, and acting against any Guild attempts to use competition between them to drive down their commissions.<br /> <br /> \u200bProbably works best as a very recent initiative, most likely within the last five years, so that the thrust of its stories would be in active recruitment and dealing with the initial response by the Guild, rather than being an established element (unless one specifically wanted that to be a detail of the manner in which the Guild in the Scavenger Lands commissions the services of Dragon Blooded).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T11:08:16-07:00","id":1204629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204622#post1204622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIdea: a group of outcastes based out of the Scavenger Lands who, recognising the value of their services to the Guild and the frequency with which lone Exalted get hired by them, intend to function as a kind of union to give them collective bargaining power with the Guild (at least insofar as they have contacts with the Dirctorate, and what are sure to be some of the more prominent factors and Guild councils), establishing standards by which they're treated, and acting against any Guild attempts to use competition between them to drive down their commissions.<br /> <br /> \u200bProbably works best as a very recent initiative, most likely within the last five years, so that the thrust of its stories would be in active recruitment and dealing with the initial response by the Guild, rather than being an established element (unless one specifically wanted that to be a detail of the manner in which the Guild in the Scavenger Lands commissions the services of Dragon Blooded).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, I never thought union politics would go with Dragonblooded. I like it. <br /> I should note that I've left out a general rule that almost every threshold region I've had has a Dragonblooded family running some state or 2. Usually the states the players are in but not always. For instance, I have a northern group of kingdoms, nameless, where Dragonblooded Smiths have established themselves as nobility, built a poperty system by which the creator of the tool has ultimate ownership of it (so the farmers rent their plows from the smiths), and engage in the occasional war amongst their states because their city states and that happens when their not fighting off the damned mountain nomads.<br /> <br /> Or the Jundun, who recently united. A theoacracy, the Jund believe that at the end of time the Lords of fire will burn the forest of the dead, so they must bury their dead in stone coffins to join the firefighters of the Huntsman of the Charnel Wood (who is a deathlord. Yes I frequently have society's who's funerary rites assist the deathlords in getting more ghosts).Sorcerous workings by the smaller cult of the Deep has resulted in amphibous and fishman like Dragonblooded, who were really handy in their naval campaigns against nearby powers.<br /> <br /> Sometime today I'm going to flesh out some Dragonblooded that have established themselves in Malfeas. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T14:36:39-07:00","id":1204695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204486#post1204486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y<br /> \u200bSo it feels kind of odd that for many people, their first response when it comes to devising groups of their own is &quot;serve the Lunar Exalted&quot;. Like, not even a particular kind of thing that they might do for them, that emphasizes unique skills, just serve a Celestial Exalt, and maybe be beastfolk.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be one thing if it was a group that were a Lunar's actual children, maybe from a backstory of that Lunar also being somebody with the Dragon's blood (possibly even a former member of the Scarlet Dynasty) who paired up with another outcaste, but no, they're &quot;loyalists&quot;, soooo I take it that they're supposed to have been under a Lunar since the Usurpation?<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do they get out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think people's minds go there because it's natural counter-extreme that logically would exist in the setting with bloodline based Exalted. I think it highlights the contrast rather than undermines Dragon-Blooded themes.<br /> <br /> With the Komodo-Dragon-Men of the Caul, I'm imagining they have a religion based around the union of Gaia of Luna, and via their alliance with the Lunar Exalted, get to enjoy the benefits of the Caul for Dragon-Blooded without the continuous assault Dynast pilgrims endure - a sign of the blessed union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T14:51:26-07:00","id":1204696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204186#post1204186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the game I ran until recently (and now my friend's running) has two main Outcaste groups.<br /> <br /> One is a country called Varamaya, where humans are split into 5 social castes, one for each aspect, led by a small number of DBs of that aspect.<br /> So the Tree Caste are vegetarian, pacifist polyamorous farmers;<br /> The Flame Caste are ecstatic warrior-berzerkers and butchers;<br /> The Wind Caste are artisans;<br /> The River Caste are river traders (the country is surrounded by many rivers and lakes);<br /> The Stone Caste are labourers and miners.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of something similar with coequal tribes. None of them should be &quot;the warriors&quot; for my purposes, since ritual combat between the tribes is part of their culture, so i'm still fiddling with their areas of dominance.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking my River Tribe will be the farmers - tied to the river valley and its annual flooding.<br /> The Wind Tribe are nomadic pasturalists - herdsmen, shepherds, and butchers.<br /> The Stone Tribe are the miners and masons.<br /> The Forest Tribe are the hunter-gatherers and guardians of the borderlands<br /> And the Flame Tribe keeps the secrets of metallurgy.<br /> <br /> I haven't decided where they're territory is, but it needs to be in the FAAAARRRR Threshold. I'm leaning toward a fertile volcanic river valley in the far southwest mountains unless I come up with a better idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T14:54:39-07:00","id":1204697,"title":"","content":"A large volcanic river valley would be a good place for a society where each tribe has an elemental obsession, as it has a variety of terrain types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T15:03:16-07:00","id":1204701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204695#post1204695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think people's minds go there because it's natural counter-extreme that logically would exist in the setting with bloodline based Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat is the significance of their being bloodline based?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Komodo-Dragon-Men of the Caul, I'm imagining they have a religion based around the union of Gaia of Luna, and via their alliance with the Lunar Exalted, get to enjoy the benefits of the Caul for Dragon-Blooded without the continuous assault Dynast pilgrims endure - a sign of the blessed union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok, now I'll cop to something; I actually <i>did</i> read that idea of them being on the Caul at first, and think that if there was anywhere that there was going to be such a union, that would be one that made sense.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen I came back to it after a couple of nights sleep, and forget that detail in the course of forming an argument against the familiar narrative of Dragon Blooded in dedicated service to Lunars. The combination of expectation and some early morning haze, probably with rumination on the subject having been one of the things that I feel asleep to.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd this idea that you're presenting here, of a synthesis of the spiritual significance that they place holds to both Lunars and Terrestrials, and the practical significance of having easier access to the pilgrimage route, is one that I think issss pretty great as the basis of an outcaste tradition in general, and one that might have a more positive relationship with Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Particularly if the landscape of prominent Lunars on the Caul is frequently changing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T15:20:23-07:00","id":1204704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204701#post1204701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhat is the significance of their being bloodline based?</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuous cultural identity and territory over generations, allowing for a major divergent group from Creation's norm to maintain itself. Also with Beastmen you have the factor of being hated by the Shogunate-heirs for being seen as Anathema-blooded already built in too.<br /> <br /> I should stress that the reason is I want at least one group that are Lunar-aligned Beastmen is not because I want so badly to play that - but because I want to play a Dragon-Blooded Beastman, who feels his tribe's Lunar forebearer is a tyrant, and runs off and joins with the Vermillion Legion - so there's a Fire Aspect Bat-person in Legion armor trying to prove himself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T15:21:19-07:00","id":1204705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204701#post1204701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhat is the significance of their being bloodline based?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aristocracy and rulership. Dragonblooded in service of Solar/Lunars/Infernals/Abyssals/Not Them feels reversed. I expect inherited powers to result in them being in charge, and trying to kill anathema (has anyone played a Celestial in service of Dragonblooded by the way?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T15:29:43-07:00","id":1204706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204593#post1204593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never mind all that, tell me more about your idea of a city of martial artists being host to a tradition of Dragon Blooded!</div> </div> </div> </div>*whistles* Well, if you insist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Don't have a firm concept for this yet, but I do love speculating and throwing stuff together as I slowly go.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda split between the spirituality tropes and the more humble, raw, practical side. So I'm thinking of splitting the difference! An ancient, holy, revered site, that once upon a time was this isolated serene grand dojo.... but times change. Cities build around places of value, and sometimes, one of the most valuable things is protection. So what was once this remote commune, a pilgrimage spot has become a bustling settlement, with wooden buildings and huts beside graceful pagodas and children playing around statues of ancient, forgotten heroes. There's playhouses, an inn or two, and at least one big arena where you can reliably find young martial artists showing their best moves against their rivals<br /> <br /> Going for some more specifics on the MA tradition.... I'm thinking the Outcastes have formed several orders. There's one ancient, very revered group that claim descent from the original monastic order that founded the place. But over the years, as the settlement grew, members of the old order forged their own path, their own style and philosophy, or came to the area from far away. Some gurus have set up shop actually within the town, some in relatively close proximity, so they can have the peace and quiet of isolation while still being close enough to recruit acolytes and purchase supplies. The town's run by an elected reeve, but military defence or anything similarly serious comes before a council of every group's Master. And they don't always see eye to eye.<br /> <br /> The issue of bloodline is kinda thorny. Any dojo will accept anyone, but it's known that the Blood of the Dragons is the mark of someone destined for greatness. Thus the children and grandchildren of famous masters are watched closely. Marriage between members of different schools is fairly common, though generally that's between <i>allied </i>schools. A child moving away from the monastic life in favour of secular work is fairly common and usually accepted, even if the child is Dragon Blooded (although with reluctance in that case) Switching schools, and joining the community of another is touchy diplomatic ground that tends to flare rivalries to breaking point.<br /> <br /> What underpins these schools philosophically? Why was the original monastery founded in the first place? I have some ideas. Will continue trying to flesh this out later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T15:33:24-07:00","id":1204707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204705#post1204705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aristocracy and rulership. Dragonblooded in service of Solar/Lunars/Infernals/Abyssals/Not Them feels reversed. I expect inherited powers to result in them being in charge, and trying to kill anathema (has anyone played a Celestial in service of Dragonblooded by the way?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sidereal advisor/sifu, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T15:46:55-07:00","id":1204709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204705#post1204705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(has anyone played a Celestial in service of Dragonblooded by the way?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Does adoptive daughter count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:01:03-07:00","id":1204716,"title":"","content":"I remember someone in the Headcanon thread had an idea of groups of Dragon-bloods living near the Elemental Poles, and they're spiritual cults that venerate and protect the Poles themselves. I always really liked that idea that these guys forsake all wordly Realm stuff and draw immense power from the Poles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:33:13-07:00","id":1204731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204706#post1204706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ancient, holy, revered site, that once upon a time was this isolated serene grand dojo.... but times change. Cities build around places of value, and sometimes, one of the most valuable things is protection. So what was once this remote commune, a pilgrimage spot has become a bustling settlement, with wooden buildings and huts beside graceful pagodas and children playing around statues of ancient, forgotten heroes. There's playhouses, an inn or two, and at least one big arena where you can reliably find young martial artists showing their best moves against their rivals</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOhh I like that. I'm often a fan of the settlement or system that builds up in an impromptu fashion, plus the idea of urban sprawl kind of gradually burying a major landmark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T22:52:40-07:00","id":1204798,"title":"","content":"This is only the very seed of an idea here, it is very unformed...<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about the portrayal of groups like the Amazons/Black Furies and the association of the mystical and feminine... and how in the context of the Realm, it's the masculine that is &quot;other&quot; from socially normative. So what would an all-male separatist group differentiated from the context of the matriarchy of the Realm look like?<br /> <br /> Well, in the culture of the Realm, men are associated with emotionality. &quot;Proper&quot; men are stoic to keep themselves in line - but men's inherent nature if not properly enlightened is to be ruled by their passions (same reason Fire Aspects regardless of sex are also associated with stoicism).<br /> <br /> So mystical masculinity in contrast with what's socially normative for the Realm would be all about embracing passion and exploring the interconnection of essence and the pure expression of emotion.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining that while this order/tribe is based out of... some kind of isolated stronghold, perhaps a former Immaculate monestary, or Shogunate era redoubt... their members take turns exploring the world trying to achieve great joys, anguishes, desires, etc, as the key to refining their Essence. I could even give them a Sorcery Initiation based around it!<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> Edit: Damn it... these guys are going to end up looking like the cast of 300 aren't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-09-2018, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T02:38:17-07:00","id":1204816,"title":"","content":"So I was re inspired to do some Terrestial exalted that instead of having the Dragon as mythology beast as a unifing theme had other beasts/monsters<br /> <br /> Like<br /> The Kraken-Blooded<br /> <br /> Yeti-kin<br /> <br /> Manticorian<br /> <br /> Pegasus-bloods/cousins<br /> <br /> Jotunn-brood<br /> <br /> Still with Elemental powers, but with nation centers closer to the other poles than earth. Each have an small nation, building to rival the Realm, but being called Shogunate, The Blue Union, Blessed Baronies Confederation... with overhead titles different from emperor or empress... so maybe T'zar (I know it is basically the same, but this i Exalted), Maharaja, Sultan (maybe even Kaiser). Each being either Former Realm legions (like lookshy), isolated since the Usurpation or newly created with no prior knowledge of other exaltation than their own nations.<br /> <br /> So like the Kraken-Blooded is trying to make their Pole (in this case water) the center pole of creation, rearranging the rest of it. Others want to usurp the realm (Jotunn-blooded), or created a rivalling empire that spreads from their own pole towards the rest of Creation (Manticorian)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","user":"light-hero","date":". 04-09-2018, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T03:27:45-07:00","id":1204825,"title":"","content":"I have an idea I am developing for an Outcaste group. the are a set of sorcerer poet-kings. Obsessed with a functional type of immortality to retain their youth. They rule a kingdom in the east but towards the northern shore of the dreaming sea. They rule fairly to the peasants. Taxes are light comparatively to most kingdoms and each citizen is required to give a season of work every two years to the kingdom. The DB use this labor force as a way to build public works and defensive structures. Due to having a dozen or so of the DB be sorcerers. They invest heavily in sorcerous workings and due to this have rather impressive infrastructure and defenses foe the country as a whole. they have an outpost on their border where the guild is allowed to bring caravans by to trade with the kingdom. They local spirit courts of the kingdom are under the DB control as well but they work together well for the most part. Manse Fortresses defend key points in their country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T16:08:26-07:00","id":1205001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204798#post1204798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only the very seed of an idea here, it is very unformed...<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about the portrayal of groups like the Amazons/Black Furies and the association of the mystical and feminine... and how in the context of the Realm, it's the masculine that is &amp;quot;other&amp;quot; from socially normative. So what would an all-male separatist group differentiated from the context of the matriarchy of the Realm look like?<br /> <br /> Well, in the culture of the Realm, men are associated with emotionality. &amp;quot;Proper&amp;quot; men are stoic to keep themselves in line - but men's inherent nature if not properly enlightened is to be ruled by their passions (same reason Fire Aspects regardless of sex are also associated with stoicism).<br /> <br /> So mystical masculinity in contrast with what's socially normative for the Realm would be all about embracing passion and exploring the interconnection of essence and the pure expression of emotion.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining that while this order/tribe is based out of... some kind of isolated stronghold, perhaps a former Immaculate monestary, or Shogunate era redoubt... their members take turns exploring the world trying to achieve great joys, anguishes, desires, etc, as the key to refining their Essence. I could even give them a Sorcery Initiation based around it!<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> Edit: Damn it... these guys are going to end up looking like the cast of 300 aren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m calling them the Sons of Tarum. Any suggestion on where in Creation to locate them?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to put them on an island in the West. I know that\u2019s the easiest answer, but being surrounded by normative patriarchy defeats the point here.<br /> <br /> I know the River Province/Scavenger Lands is a bit crowded with Outcaste groups compared to other regions, but it is one of the most populous regions of Creation. I was thinking of their stronghold being in the same mountain range as Greyfalls (within range of Metagalapan raids). That puts them both far from the Realm, but in nominally Realm controlled territory to be a subject of weird exotic fascination to the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:17:14-07:00","id":1205033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1204696#post1204696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm thinking of something similar with coequal tribes. None of them should be &amp;quot;the warriors&amp;quot; for my purposes, since ritual combat between the tribes is part of their culture, so i'm still fiddling with their areas of dominance.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking my River Tribe will be the farmers - tied to the river valley and its annual flooding.<br /> The Wind Tribe are nomadic pasturalists - herdsmen, shepherds, and butchers.<br /> The Stone Tribe are the miners and masons.<br /> The Forest Tribe are the hunter-gatherers and guardians of the borderlands<br /> And the Flame Tribe keeps the secrets of metallurgy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then everything changed when the Flame Tribe attacked....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:27:55-07:00","id":1205035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1205033#post1205033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then everything changed when the Flame Tribe attacked....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking about how much of a martial advantage they'd have, but with all 5 tribes having Dragon-Blooded, they wouldn't be able to simply use the unilaterally force of wielding iron to extract the food and other resources they need. Even without equal weapons, the other Exalted would be able to put up too much of a fight. So they have to share their tools and weapons in return for other resources. They have a slight advantage holding back the best artifacts for themselves, but not a massive one. I'm thinking to balance that out a bit, the River-Tribe controls a Sorcery Initiation (tied to terraforming the land, they have the most use for Shaping), and the Wind Tribe (thanks to cultural exchange with outsiders, as the migrational nomads with their herds) hold the secret of Martial Arts training. No ideas as to any special advantages for the Stone and Forest Tribes.<br /> <br /> (yes, I know the reference you were making)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-09-2018, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T22:31:54-07:00","id":1206287,"title":"","content":"So, I'm working on 'clans in Malfeas' as a concept, and is it hokey to have them attribute/emulate elemental Yozis instead of dragons? (Air to Adjoran, Earth to Quaf, Fire to Malfeas, Water to Kimbery, Wood to Szorney)? Or would 2nd/3rd circle emulations be better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:18:53-07:00","id":1206298,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about a small patch of Eastern Creation that served as an experimental plant breeding facility in the Shogunate. It was isolated and top-secret enough that it managed to avoid the Great Contagion before the Wyld invasion. Staffed by a few dozen mortal servants and laborers, maybe six or seven Wood-Aspect Dragon-Blooded, some Wood Elementals, and a pair of Raptok Dragon Kings (the daimyo in whose domain this facility was located was slightly more friendly to Dragon Kings than the Shogunate at large), the combined the sorcery, Charms, and Paths of its inhabitants, as well some ingeniously designed jade-infused plant life, allowed it avoid succumbing to the Wyld and the depredations of local fae until this very day. Naturally, with all the Wood Essence around, over the centuries all of these different bloodlines entangled, and the remaining survivors (maybe 30; a high birthrate is countered by high attrition against fae raiders) are all Terrestrial Exalted with literal Blood of the Dragon (Kings) in them. Most, of course, are Wood Aspected, but there is one Earth Aspect and a few Water. <br /> <br /> Recently, a Guild slave caravan chanced upon their island of Creation, awakening curiosity about the wider world they've been cut off from for so long. A few are now contemplating leading the remainders of the caravan (they slew the master and most of the guards and freed the slaves) back to Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:59:31-07:00","id":1206305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1206287#post1206287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm working on 'clans in Malfeas' as a concept, and is it hokey to have them attribute/emulate elemental Yozis instead of dragons? (Air to Adjoran, Earth to Quaf, Fire to Malfeas, Water to Kimbery, Wood to Szorney)? Or would 2nd/3rd circle emulations be better?</div> </div> </div> </div>well, I once toyed with the idea that the dragons were &quot;fathered&quot; by other Primordials, so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T10:41:20-07:00","id":1208492,"title":"","content":"So the most recent Realm preview does have a reference to an individual Dragon-Blooded Parrot-man whose people were whipped out by Fair Folk, and joined the Immaculate Order after. That's not unlike my desire to play a Fire Aspect Bat-person who enlists with the Vermillion Legion.<br /> <br /> Right now I've refined my concepts for 3 groups of DB Beastmen so none of them are under Lunar domination, because that type of society of Exalted doesn't last.<br /> <br /> - Bat-people in the jungles of the Southeast, loosely inspired by the Blood Bats of 2nd Edition. They WERE a case of a Lunar dominated weaponized DBs... which resulted in a dead Lunar.<br /> <br /> - A Caul based tribe with a more symbiotic relationship with Lunars, rather than being actively dominated by a forbearer. I'm thinking Komodo Dragons, but I'm open to other ideas.<br /> <br /> - Kireeki worshipping dolphin-people + pelagrathope society created to patrol for signs of the returning Spoken back in the First Age, who's society revolves around besting one another as hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T11:02:30-07:00","id":1208495,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... an idea has suddenly occurred to me...<br /> <br /> \u200bI said before about a Lunar being the child of some Dragon Blooded, possibly Dynasts, who hooked up with another Terrestrial and had a bunch of Dragon Blooded children (I'd say that bloodline can get one to around half Exalted, so maybe five or six sired over the course of a couple hundred years), and then they do things a lot like what Lunars might do with their Moon-touched children. Not even necessarily Silver Pact stuff; it would be fairly fitting for one of those Lunars off doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow I've got an image in which the Lunar is long gone, killed by the Wyld Hunt, and their surviving children, plus their children and grandchildren, have a grudge against the Realm. Probably not on a <i>very</i> long timeline, just back enough to have the members of the family at the top still remember their beloved parent and galled at the injustice of Immaculates killing them, who can influence their own offspring in the direction of doing something to undermine the Realm. Not a very large group, and should definitely have something going for them besides their old feud, but it's a picture I have for how the idea of Dragon Blooded loyal to a Lunar could have a twist.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor one thing, that they might maintain some traditions preserving Lunar tactics that were taught by the parent with regards to infiltration and sabotage. I'm seeing an occasion in which one member of the family went and joined up with an Imperial legion, waited for an opportunity in which they could sabotage the unit under their command in a manner that caused the legion severe trouble, and then disappeared.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's... probably not entirely practical, if I should look back at how outcastes are recruited for the legions. If they only take found eggs who could be trained at Pasiap's Stair, then it's a lot of time and effort to put in, not to mention the risk, just to only really be in a position to hurt one legion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T13:08:05-07:00","id":1208539,"title":"","content":"The larceny charm Terrifying Forest-Devil Mask give me an idea. What about a very little group of outcaste, a family line who's history's build around the figure of a legendary local Hero (like . Everybody think he is immortal but in fact, this is a figure that pass from generation to generation, the thin-blood of the family not habitually allowing them to have more than one or two dragon-blooded at the time.<br /> <br /> I imagine the mortals of the family know the secret and help the hero in many ways. What could be fun is if a second member of the family exalt, one who have different views about the decision the Hero must make. It could bring some cool vendetta stories.<br /> <br /> (Since it's my first participation, I juste wan't to say that I'm a regular reader of this forum since a good year now and I like all the ambiance in here. You're all full of creativity and cool ideas, and you seem to respect each others a lot in your conversations, it's a pleasure to read you !)<br /> <br /> Also english is not my native language and I don't no yet how to write that in my sign so sorry for my grammar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13634-mrcroquemitaine","user":"MrCroquemitaine","date":". 04-18-2018, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13634-mrcroquemitaine","name":"MrCroquemitaine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13634_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T14:18:08-07:00","id":1208571,"title":"","content":"An interesting idea that's at least somewhat undercut with 3E's Progenitive essence concept, but I'd always had an image of a DB kingdom that basically doesn't believe in the &quot;bloodline purity&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Basically extended clans of dozens of kids in order to try to play the numbers game and assume that the more chances to Exalt, the better overall average they'll have. Of course, the progenitive essence thing kinda undermines that, but originally their problem was that when any given DB dies, their estates and so on are likely to be carved up among a dozen heirs at the least, probably twice or more that. That and while they're located in the North in a rather nice space of farmable land due to a sorcerous working, the extent that the terraforming is progressing outwards is far too slow to manage their population. So either they start working on trying to conquer their neighbors (having the only large scale farmland in the area has made them a lot of allies nicely up until now) or they start having social breakdowns inside their borders as the younger scions start fighting over who gets what little there's left to own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T17:15:28-07:00","id":1208632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrCroquemitaine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1208539#post1208539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The larceny charm Terrifying Forest-Devil Mask give me an idea. What about a very little group of outcaste, a family line who's history's build around the figure of a legendary local Hero (like . Everybody think he is immortal but in fact, this is a figure that pass from generation to generation, the thin-blood of the family not habitually allowing them to have more than one or two dragon-blooded at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA kind of Exalted version of the Phantom, and a different take on the approach to Chosen in the roles of local culture heroes. It sounds neat, and an interesting way in which a bloodline might maximize the impact of the limited Terrestrials it produces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrCroquemitaine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could be fun is if a second member of the family exalt, one who have different views about the decision the Hero must make. It could bring some cool vendetta stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat <i>does</i> sound fun. Legacy heroes having rivalries or schisms based on who gets to carry the mantle or what the meaning of it is can be one of the more compelling things that is done with such heroic identities, and the backstory that you're postulating creates this nice image of the family being completely shaken by an unprecedented situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrCroquemitaine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also english is not my native language and I don't no yet how to write that in my sign so sorry for my grammar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's pretty good; the errors are minor, and the sentence structure is all accurate, so it's quite easy to read. Don't worry about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T10:37:48-08:00","id":1429524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203915-what-are-your-outcaste-groups?p=1208632#post1208632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, it's pretty good; the errors are minor, and the sentence structure is all accurate, so it's quite easy to read. Don't worry about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny because when you speak French natively, it's pretty obvious that he and I are from France, because the structure of our sentences are first thought out in French and then put into English.<br /> <br /> Which makes me think, there totally should be a Linguistic Charm that let you know where someone comes from just by hearing him. I guess a Solar version would allow you to speak in sentences that only this person could understand the meaning, while to outlooks it seems like a regular conversation (I think there is a Lore Charm that looks like this ?). for a DB, it would probably allow you to gain a specialty in the regional culture the person is from, that you can then use with said person in future rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T16:59:24-08:00","id":1430003,"title":"","content":"No big ideas, truth be told. Might redo my homebrewed cadet house from previous editions, the Sinasi, to better fit with their portrayal as &quot;dynasts gone native&quot; ruling their own pieces of Threshold - something me and my friends sort of glossed over, not to say completely ignored, while writing them back in late 1e/early 2e.<br /> <br /> (Kind of justified in that they were actually a branch of the Iselsi - or worse - completely faking it, but i digress)<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing that comes to mind, somewhat inspired by Rutanjali from Aspectbook: Wood - is the idea of a dragon-blooded outcaste so immersed in the interactions of one or more elemental courts that the line between exalted and spirit has been blurred many times over and forgotten between long-lived heroes and mortal descendants ascended into godhood through the eras.<br /> <br /> Maybe some lone dragon-blooded sorcerer that went really stir-crazy playing with demon and elemental summoning both in isolation, leading to sybaritic debauchery and all kinds of peculiar experiments and strangeness, that take on a life and direction of its own after centuries of service even after the founder's demise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-19-2024, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}